Subject: Cantor Runtime Closure Materialization Plan P0 Delineation

@ [delineation_uuid] fa983a39-45fb-49ec-bffd-25ef2fb69d35
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] dc7d8d88-83bd-4f0c-bc2a-6973afa99700

& [Declaration]
  + RIS-P0 says what runtime closure is expected and how its supplied declaration deterministically compiles

& [Planning]
  + this P0-to-P1 seam says what future material work would be ordered, why it remains unresolved, which exact P0 identity it serves and which denied capabilities it would require

& [Execution]
  + a later RIS-P1 executor alone may observe prerequisites reacquire sources build create directories stage bytes set permissions verify physical bytes prepare rollback or issue an observation receipt

& [HostAndArtifacts]
  + RIS-P2 alone selects supported host tuple toolchain resolver transport artifact pack provider model license and compatibility profiles

& [Activation]
  + RIS-P3 alone starts services admits health recognizes generations activates rolls back or exposes operator runtime state

& [NonSubstitution]
  + plan compiled is never material present, operation proposed is never operation authorized, expected digest is never verified byte, receipt candidate is never installation receipt and synthetic fixture is never real deployment evidence
